  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "Ready each friendly ADEPTUS CUSTODES unit that has Martial Ka’tah when your Command phase starts. A readied unit may use one Ka’tah at the listed time, then loses its readied state. As the Fight phase begins, Dacatarai lets the chosen unit re-roll melee Hit rolls that show 1 against enemies other than MONSTER or VEHICLE units. At that phase’s start, Kaptaris gives incoming melee attacks against the chosen unit −1 to hit. Rendax gives the chosen unit [LETHAL HITS: MONSTER/VEHICLE] on melee attacks when it is picked to fight. In your Command phase, Conversai lets a chosen unit start an action despite being engaged or battle-shocked, and stay eligible to shoot despite starting an action, through turn end. As you pick a unit to move in your Movement phase, Calistus lets its models pass through all other models on a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move. As you pick a unit to shoot in your Shooting phase, Salvus lets it ignore modifiers to BS and to its hit and wound rolls.",
